This project is a file-based bank account management system developed using the C programming language. It demonstrates the use of random-access files, allowing efficient storage, retrieval, and modification of account records.
The system simulates basic banking operations such as creating accounts, updating balances, deleting records, searching accounts, and exporting data to a readable format.

Concepts Used:
1.Structures (struct)
2.File handling in C
3.Random access files
4.Binary file operations
5.String handling (strcmp)
6.Menu-driven programming

Technologies:
    1.Language: C
    2.Compiler: GCC / Turbo C / Any standard C compiler
    3.File System: Binary file (credit.dat)

Learning Outcome
This project helps in understanding:

     1.How real-world banking systems manage data
     2.Efficient file handling techniques in C
     3.Implementation of CRUD operations using binary files
